; An external report destination that has NOT authorised dmarc.test.
;
; The zone exists and answers, so the absence of the authorization record is a
; real NXDOMAIN rather than an unreachable server. That distinction matters: one
; is a misconfiguration, the other is "we could not tell".
$ORIGIN unauth-reports.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.
@       IN TXT  "a real zone, deliberately missing the _report._dmarc authorization"
